{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792482299,"nonce":"sesgaq4q4ybouzeV2k9osFMX+bM=","message":"The synchronous native host entry now routes f64 parameters through the compiler's typed scalar ABI bridge, including mixed argument order and floating returns. Integer-only entry trampolines retain their existing arity support. Host calls validate exact arity, values and null entry pointers; unsupported f32-parameter and larger mixed signatures return errors before native invocation. Pointer arguments accept pointer/raw-address/null values, and pointer results are preserved instead of discarded. Typed boolean returns read the return byte.\n\nLocal ARM64 macOS validation: cargo test -p zyntax_embed --lib --test embed_tests --offline passed 83 library tests and 104 integration tests, including five new scalar ABI regressions. cargo clippy -p zyntax_embed --lib --tests --offline passed. The native TypeScript integration test passed interpreted, Cranelift and installed LLVM execution (LLVM 21; LLVM_SYS_211_PREFIX=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm cargo test -p zyntax_ts --features llvm-backend --test tiers --offline). It confirms no native functions at initial load and correct score values across tier changes. These are correctness checks, not performance measurements.\n\nScope is the synchronous call_native_with_signature path. The separate legacy asynchronous DynamicValue-to-pointer trampoline has not been redesigned here.","files":null}]}